# Dependencies — restored by `make install`, never committed.
backend/.venv/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
frontend/out/

# Secrets. The `*.example` files are committed and are the documentation; the
# filled copies beside them never are. `!` after a broad rule rather than a
# narrower rule above it, because git applies the last pattern that matches.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.deploy.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local capture output, if anything is ever written outside object storage.
/tmp/
scratch/

# Credential vault: session cookies, CSRF tokens, whatever a login produced.
# On disk so the services work; never in history.
backend/.sro-vault
backend/worker.log

# Subagent-driven-development scratch (ledgers, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Google OAuth client secrets, as downloaded from the Cloud console. The file
# name is whatever Google called it, so the pattern matches the shape rather
# than one name -- a secret that only stays out of git while somebody remembers
# to rename it is a secret already halfway into git.
client_secret*.json
.gmail-token.json
# One Google grant per tenant, each named by the sha256 of the bearer that
# reaches it. Refresh tokens: never committed.
backend/.gmail-grants/

# ...and the same shapes after somebody renames one. The two patterns above
# were already here, with the comment above them, and three real credential
# files still sat untracked in backend/ -- `old-client_secret_...json.disabled`
# and `.gmail-token.json.old-client`. A prefix and a suffix were enough to walk
# past both. Anchored patterns guard the name a file was downloaded with; these
# guard the shape it keeps after being renamed out of the way.
*client_secret*
*gmail-token*

# Named individually because the name says nothing: a real Google OAuth token
# saved from an editor's "save as" with the default filename.
backend/Untitled

# The mutation run's working copy: mutmut rewrites the whole tree into here,
# one file per mutant, and the cache beside it. Regenerated by `make mutants`.
backend/mutants/

# The Playwright MCP browser's console capture. Written by the tool, not by
# this repository, and it grows without bound: the one found here was 6.7 MB of
# the rig's own status page retrying against a server that was not running,
# 73,170 times. Nothing in it but localhost, but an untracked multi-megabyte log
# of a browser session is exactly what a careless `git add -A` sweeps up.
.playwright-mcp/

# The rig's own capture stores and the artifacts beside them. These hold live
# customer WMS payloads -- the same evidence the redaction work all session was
# protecting -- and they were untracked but NOT ignored, which is one
# `git add -A` away from committing a database of it. The artifacts directory
# is named twice because the ingest route resolves it from settings().db_path,
# so a rig started from the repo root writes it here.
rig.db
rig.db-wal
rig.db-shm
rig.db.bak*
artifacts/
# Per-model copies of the store a bake-off works on: 23MB each, regenerated
# by every sweep, and the sweep's own findings live in the store the API
# serves rather than here.

# Deleted from the tree on 2026-09-14, the last item on the rig-into-the-backend
# deletion list, and kept in full on the branch `backup/the-rig`. What is left
# here on a working machine is one person's residue -- an `.env` holding real
# keys, `rig.db` holding captured evidence, caches and bake-off output. None of
# it is deleted for anybody, and none of it is ever committed back by a stray
# `git add -A`.
new_agent_arch/
# Eval cases and results hold operator data: never committed. The redacted set is backend/evals/ci/.
backend/evals/cases/
backend/evals/results/
backend/evals/candidates/
backend/evals/proposals/

# The Chrome Web Store zip (make package-extension)
/dist/
